==================================================
FRONTEND ARCHITECTURE
=====================

Use reusable components.

Suggested structure:

src/

components/
common/
public/
admin/
booking/
rooms/
dashboard/

pages/
public/
admin/

layouts/
PublicLayout.jsx
AdminLayout.jsx

services/
api.js

data/
mockRooms.js
mockBookings.js
mockCustomers.js
mockPayments.js

hooks/

utils/

types/

The public and admin layouts must be completely separate.

==================================================
API READY ARCHITECTURE
======================

Create an API service abstraction.

For now:

api.js

Use mock data.

Structure functions such as:

getRooms()
getRoom(id)
searchAvailableRooms()
createBooking(data)
getBooking(id)
getMyBookings()
getBookings()
getCustomers()
getPayments()
getDashboardStats()

Later these functions will call FastAPI endpoints.

Do not put API logic directly inside page components.

==================================================
RESPONSIVE DESIGN
=================

Desktop:

* Full sidebar admin
* Multi-column room cards
* Sticky booking panel

Tablet:

* Reduced columns
* Collapsible filters

Mobile:

* Bottom-friendly navigation
* Hamburger menu
* Single-column cards
* Filter drawer
* Sticky booking CTA
* Large touch targets
* No horizontal scrolling

Test every page at:

320px
375px
768px
1024px
1440px

==================================================
UX REQUIREMENTS
===============

Prioritize:

1. Simple navigation
2. Clear booking CTA
3. Fast room discovery
4. Easy date selection
5. Clear pricing
6. Clear availability
7. Minimal booking steps
8. Strong mobile experience
9. Accessible forms
10. Clear success/error feedback

Never hide important information behind unnecessary interactions.

Pricing should always clearly show:

Price per night
Number of nights
Taxes
Total

==================================================
IMPORTANT TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS
================================

Use:

React
Vite
Tailwind CSS
React Router
Lucide React
React Hook Form

Use functional components.

Use reusable components.

Avoid unnecessary dependencies.

Use clean semantic HTML.

Use accessible buttons, labels and form fields.

Do not hardcode repeated UI.

Do not create backend code.

Do not create authentication backend.

Use mock authentication state for admin screens.

Make the code easy to connect to FastAPI later.

Finally, ensure the entire project runs with:

npm install
npm run dev

and contains no broken routes, missing imports or console errors.
